**ANSI C** (the constants `ROW`, `COL` and the subprogram `row_line` of Task 2 are in the same file, before these subprograms):

```c
void print_rows(int X[][COL], int row, int col)
{
    int i, j;

    for (i = 0; i < row; i++) {
        row_line();
        for (j = 0; j < col; j++)
            printf("|  %d  ", X[i][j]);      /* a bar, two spaces, the value, two spaces */
        printf("|");                         /* final bar (no new line: row_line() starts one) */
    }
    row_line();
}

void PrintMat(int A[][COL], int row, int col)
{
    printf("Initial Stage:");
    print_rows(A, row, col);
}

void PrintNextGen(int B[][COL], int row, int col)
{
    printf("Next Generation:");
    print_rows(B, row, col);
}
```

**Layout.** Each value takes six characters: the bar, two spaces, the digit and two spaces; `row_line()` prints one space and five dashes per column, so the dashes lie between the bars. The second bar of each pair is the first of the next value, and the last bar closes the row.

