The calls are made in this order: seed the generator, fill the board `A`, display it, compute the next generation into `B`, display `B`. `NextGen(A,B)` of the statement is the subprogram `Next_Gen(A, B)` of Task 2, question 5. By Figure 2 the seed must satisfy 0 < s < 16, so the main program asks for the seed again until it is valid.

**Algorithm**

```
