Hand check of the second row of the next generation: the cell (row 1, column 0) is dead and has three live neighbours (column 1 of rows 0, 1 and 2), so it is born (1); the cell (1, 1) is alive with two live neighbours (above and below), so it lives on (1); the cell (0, 1), on the edge, has only one live neighbour, so it dies (0); the cell (1, 2), dead, has six live neighbours, so it stays dead (0). This agrees with the display. The vertical stripes come from the generator, whose output alternates 0 and 1 (see Task 2, question 2).

**Marking:** the five calls in the right order (2); the seed respects 0 < s < 16 (1).
